From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiago Medicci <tiago.medicci@espressif.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] configure: disable Python venv for meson

QEMU's private virtual environment tries to install Meson and pycotap,
which is incompatible with OpenEmbedded's offline --disable-download
build. OpenEmbedded already provides supported Python and Meson versions,
so use those directly and disable the package bootstrap.

This follows the equivalent OpenEmbedded-Core QEMU workaround.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OpenEmbedded-specific]
Signed-off-by: Tiago Medicci <tiago.medicci@espressif.com>
---
 configure | 7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 3ea8cce38b..d75ee7e8c7 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -988,12 +988,9 @@ echo "python determined to be '$python'"
 echo "python version: $($python --version)"
 
-python="$($python -B "${source_path}/python/scripts/mkvenv.py" create pyvenv)"
-if test "$?" -ne 0 ; then
-    error_exit "python venv creation failed"
-fi
+# Keep $python as resolved by configure; skip venv creation (meson-native).
 
 # Suppress writing compiled files
 python="$python -B"
-mkvenv="$python ${source_path}/python/scripts/mkvenv.py"
+mkvenv=true
 
 # Finish preparing the virtual environment using vendored .whl files
